.TH "daharness" "1" "" ""
.SH NAME
daharness \(em daharness security framework services (Brain, ZAP, MSF
MCP, API gateway)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]daharness\f[R] [\f[I]\(endaemon\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the daharness service stack for authorized security research:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Brain sidecar\f[R] \(em Unix\-socket tool dispatch core; the socket
lives at \f[I]$BRAIN_SOCKET\f[R] (system profile:
\f[B]/run/daharness/brain.sock\f[R]).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]OWASP ZAP daemon\f[R] \(em API access list kept to loopback; the
browser proxy binds \f[I]$ZAP_PROXY_BIND\f[R] (default 0.0.0.0).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Metasploit RPC/MCP\f[R] \(em msfrpcd on \f[I]$MSF_RPC_PORT\f[R]
(default 55553).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]API gateway\f[R] \(em FastAPI on port 5000 (host lane), exposing
\f[I]/tools/execute\f[R], \f[I]/tools/search\f[R], \f[I]/memory/*\f[R],
\f[I]/scratch/*\f[R] and the streamable\-HTTP MCP endpoint
\f[I]/mcp\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Wordlist preflight\f[R] \(em wordlist tree sanity\-checked before
serving.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\(endaemon\f[R]
Foregrounds the services stack.
Passing it is optional \(em the interactive secretary chat loop was
trimmed from the packaged build, so bare \f[CR]daharness\f[R] behaves
identically (interactive tool lane: \f[I]daharness\-repl\f[R](1);
registry re\-index: \f[B]daharness\-index\f[R](1)).
.SH CONFIGURATION
The systemd units load \f[B]/etc/daharness/daharness.env\f[R] via
\f[I]EnvironmentFile=\f[R] (system profile: WORKSPACE_ROOT,
BRAIN_SOCKET, GATEWAY_HOST, GATEWAY_PORT, GATEWAY_API_KEY); operator
shells use the tree\(cqs \f[I].env\f[R] (\f[I]bootstrap.py\f[R],
\f[I]api_gateway.py\f[R] and \f[I]tool_repl.py\f[R] load it with
\f[I]override=True\f[R]).
See \f[B]daharness.env(5)\f[R].
.SH OPERATOR ONBOARDING (system profile)
A fresh install provisions operator access instead of leaving it to code
archaeology: \f[B]/etc/profile.d/daharness.sh\f[R] exports the
system\-profile WORKSPACE_ROOT and BRAIN_SOCKET into shells that lack
them (wrappers source it for non\-login runs), and \f[I]postinst\f[R]
grants the \f[I]daharness\f[R] group to \f[I]sudo\f[R]\-group members
\(em that group owns the state root and the brain UDS (UMask 0007), so a
sudo operator\(cqs shell shares cookie jar, scratch, findings, and the
socket with the service lane after re\-login (or
\f[CR]newgrp daharness\f[R]).
Non\-sudo operators: \f[CR]sudo usermod \-aG daharness <user>\f[R].
An operator outside the group who probes the system\-profile state sees
an honest \f[CR]lane_blocked: true\f[R] permission report from
\f[I]framework_health\f[R], never a phantom \(lqdown\(rq.
.PP
Scope manifests get the same treatment: \f[I]postinst\f[R] seeds the
editable lab template into
\f[I]/var/lib/daharness/scope/lab_local\-lab.json\f[R] (never stomping
an existing file) so a temp local\-lab scope is authored\-off\-rip \(em
edit the subnet/ROE lines, then
\f[CR]python tool_repl.py scope on local\-lab \-\-platform lab\f[R].
Custom manifests follow *scope/<platform>_<handle>.json* in the state
root and arm with any \f[CR]\-\-platform\f[R] value.
The pristine copy lives at
\f[I]/usr/share/daharness/examples/scope/lab_local\-lab.json\f[R].
.PP
Privileged lanes (raw\-socket scanning, low\-port OOB) are not part of
this baseline; they degrade honestly and are documented in
\f[B]daharness\-safety(7)\f[R].
.SH FILES
\f[I]/run/daharness/brain.sock\f[R] \(em Brain UDS (system profile)
\f[I]/var/lib/daharness/\f[R] \(em engagement state root (system
profile) \f[I]/etc/daharness/daharness.env\f[R] \(em configuration
\f[I]/etc/profile.d/daharness.sh\f[R] \(em operator\-shell plumbing
(system\-profile WORKSPACE_ROOT + BRAIN_SOCKET for shells that lack
them) \f[I]/usr/share/daharness/examples/scope/lab_local\-lab.json\f[R]
\(em editable lab scope\-manifest template (postinst seeds it into the
state root\(cqs \f[I]scope/\f[R])
